/E (Scientists have discovered that black holes of vastly different sizes appear to launch powerful jets according to the same universal rule. Black holes launch radio jets when their feeding rate drops to exactly 2% of the Eddington limit, a universal threshold that applies equally to both stellar-mass and supermassive black holes. The breakthrough could explain why some black holes suddenly erupt years after devouring a star and help astronomers predict when these spectacular outbursts will happen.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
